.TH MDC.STATFS_REFRESH 4 2026-11-07 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdc.statfs_refresh, osc.statfs_refresh, lov.statfs_refresh, lmv.statfs_refresh, obdfilter.statfs_refresh, osp.statfs_refresh, lod.statfs_refresh \- replace cached space usage of a device now
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param obdfilter." FSNAME "*.statfs_refresh=1"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param osp." FSNAME "*.statfs_refresh=1"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param lod." FSNAME "*.statfs_refresh=1"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param " "DEVICE" "." FSNAME "*.statfs_refresh=1"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Perms
.br
.BR 200 " | " --w-------
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per device
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present on
.BR obdfilter ,
.BR osp ,
.BR lod ,
.BR osc ,
.BR lov ,
.B mdc
and
.B lmv
devices
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each of these devices caches the space usage and state of the storage
below it, and reads it again only when the cached copy is older than its
maximum age.  Any write to
.B statfs_refresh
replaces the cached copy now.  The value written is ignored.
.TP
.B obdfilter
reads the space usage of the OST backing filesystem.
.TP
.B osp
sends a statfs RPC to its target and waits for the reply.  A deactivated
device is skipped.
.TP
.B lod
reads the space usage cached by each of its
.B osp
devices and recalculates the object allocation weights, rather than
waiting up to
.B qos_maxage
seconds to do so.  It does not refresh the
.B osp
devices themselves.
.TP
.BR osc ", " mdc ", " lov ", " lmv
send a statfs RPC to each target.
.PP
Each device reads the cache of the device below it, so to see a change of
OST space or state in object allocation, write
.B obdfilter
on the OSS first, then
.B osp
and
.B lod
on the MDS.  Test scripts do this in place of a sleep of
.B qos_maxage
seconds.
.PP
On
.BR osp ,
the write fails with
.B EAGAIN
at once if the target is not connected or the MDT is read only, and with
.B ETIMEDOUT
if the target does not reply within 5 seconds.  The other devices do not
wait for a target that is not connected.
.SH EXAMPLES
Make object allocation on all MDTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem use the current OST space usage:
.EX
.RB "oss# " "lctl set_param obdfilter.testfs-*.statfs_refresh=1"
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param osp.testfs-*.statfs_refresh=1"
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param lod.testfs-*.statfs_refresh=1"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B statfs_refresh
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.61
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
